# API Design

- Global prefix: `/api`, URI-based versioning (`/api/v1/users`)
- Proper status codes: POST 201, GET 200, PUT/PATCH 200, DELETE 204
- Every controller has full Swagger: `@ApiTags`, `@ApiOperation`, `@ApiResponse`, `@ApiParam`, `@ApiBearerAuth`
- Use `ParseUUIDPipe` on all `:id` route params
- `TransformInterceptor` wraps responses in `{ success: true, data, timestamp }`

## DTOs & Validation

- Every endpoint has dedicated request AND response DTOs — never pass raw Prisma types
- Use `class-validator` decorators on every field: `@IsString()`, `@IsEmail()`, `@MaxLength()`, etc.
- Use `@Exclude()` and `@Expose()` on response DTOs to control serialization
- `UpdateDto extends PartialType(OmitType(CreateDto, ['password']))` — never duplicate definitions
- Shared pagination DTO in `src/common/dto/pagination-query.dto.ts`
- `whitelist: true` and `forbidNonWhitelisted: true` in global `ValidationPipe`

## Error Handling

- Use NestJS exceptions: `NotFoundException`, `ConflictException`, `BadRequestException`, `ForbiddenException`
- NEVER throw generic `Error` or `HttpException` with magic status codes
- Business logic errors thrown in service layer, NEVER in controllers
- DB constraint violations (unique, FK) caught and re-thrown as `ConflictException`/`BadRequestException`
- Log 5xx as `logger.error` with stack trace, 4xx as `logger.warn`
